From: Harvi654 <202698022+Harvi654@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: combase: Test activation contexts in cross-apartment class-factory calls.

AI-assisted (Codex), original code; LGPL-2.1-or-later. Not submitted upstream.

Our Windows 10 x86_64/i686 MEASURE completed 48 standard-marshaled
IClassFactory calls in both STA/MTA directions. STA callbacks saw no test
marker; MTA callbacks saw the caller's current marker. Construction and
first/second marshaling markers did not select the observed callback marker.
Clients retained their context after every call.

v2 (2026-11-09): Add the Windows-derived regression and native L1 harness.
Keep the production implementation unchanged for comparison, not as a claim
that it conforms: its first-marshaling capture conflicts with the MTA
observations. This candidate is BLOCKED pending native assertion L1,
paired Wine runtime comparison and a separately reviewed scope correction.
All observed context checks are ordinary ok(); no todos hide this conflict.
The measurements are limited to IClassFactory, not every COM interface or
an inferred native propagation mechanism. No production series change.

